# claude_stop
#
# New template. Brings the arm to a controlled stop.
#
# Sending anything to port 30003 already replaces whatever script is running, so
# this stops the previous motion by existing at all - but it replaces it with
# nothing, and the arm coasts to a halt on the controller's own deceleration.
# This decelerates deliberately, at a rate the caller chooses, which is what you
# want for a soft abort that is not a protective stop.
#
# This is not a replacement for the dashboard `stop` that handle_request uses to
# cancel a goal: that one is out of band and works even when a script is wedged.
# This one is a normal request and is subject to the same admission control as
# any other, so it will be rejected while another goal is running.
#
# Optional parameters:
#   stop_acceleration (2.0) - rad/s^2.

def script():
  stopj({{ stop_acceleration | default(value=2.0) }})
  socket_send_line("stopped, q=" + to_str(get_actual_joint_positions()), "ur_driver_socket")
  return True
end
